    "rationale": "Dependency coordinates remain metadata-driven. The explicitly admitted IBE source contract, external recipe fluid-list return contract, declared recipe-builder callback arguments, the public FluidIngredient API, and the exact Ponder block-entity callback contract use canonical ABI owners after source/type proof. The nullable model-data manager family and SavedData backup/factory family require exact source owners, complete caller/provider closure, and pinned platform ABI evidence; the prepass only detects those owners and publishes their sealed inventory. Source-owned implementations retain their declarations and behavior. The native Create datagen, filtering, tag, advancement, serialization, overlay, station-map, mounted projectile, stew component, Mixin descriptor, registry-provider, player-pose, and loot families require closed source ownership and target ABI proof before mutation. The admitted project families publish with rollback; none selects a benchmark by name. These are API ownership checks, not benchmark-name switches."
